#  PURPOSE: Radboud's Disease-Gene graphing notebook
#  (radboud/2026 Radboud Disease-Gene Graphing.ipynb) hardcodes the relation
#  literal "IS_ASSOCIATED_WITH", where every other Radboud graphing notebook
#  and both other partners (Biovista, Demokritos) hardcode/emit
#  "ASSOCIATED_WITH" for the same conceptual relation. This is a copy-paste
#  inconsistency across Radboud's own notebook templates, not an intentional
#  distinct relation type — confirmed by reading the notebook source of all
#  three partners' graphing notebooks.
#
#  This patch corrects the relation label in-place on the live triple store,
#  without touching the underlying entity/disease/gene triples or dropping
#  any graphs. It follows the DELETE-not-DROP pattern documented in
#  delete_using_http.rb / purge_all_graphs.rb: the skg_loader SPARQL account
#  has write-triple privilege but no DROP/CLEAR privilege.
#
#  SCOPE: only the graph-level metadata triple
#  `?g simp:source-relation "IS_ASSOCIATED_WITH"` in the canonical metadata
#  graph <urn:simpathic:context:all_metadata> is affected. As of 2026-09-14
#  (read-only COUNT, before this patch), 40,864 graphs carry this value —
#  all of them from Radboud's Disease-Gene export
#  (radboud/graph/2026_radboud_disease-gene.nq.large), confirmed by
#  cross-tabulating relation label against simp:skg-source in the offline
#  .large export files. No other partner or relation-pair uses this literal.
#
#  RELATED FIXES (this patch covers the live database only):
#  - Utilities/Queries/JUNE_all_pairs_both_orientations_{merged,split}_evidence.csv.large
#    were already patched directly (2026-09-14) via
#    SKG_Mapping/statistics/05_results/fix_associated_with.awk, since those
#    frozen exports are what the paper's statistics and the partners' copies
#    are built from.
#  - radboud/2026 Radboud Disease-Gene Graphing.ipynb still hardcodes
#    IS_ASSOCIATED_WITH and has NOT been patched by this file. Fix with:
#      sed -i 's/IS_ASSOCIATED_WITH/ASSOCIATED_WITH/g' \
#        "radboud/2026 Radboud Disease-Gene Graphing.ipynb"
#    Without that fix, the next full notebook re-run reproduces this same
#    problem in both the live database and any freshly exported .large file.
#
#  VERIFY BEFORE: run as a plain SELECT (no auth needed, read-only) —
#    PREFIX simp: <urn:simpathic:>
#    SELECT (COUNT(?g) AS ?n) WHERE {
#      GRAPH <urn:simpathic:context:all_metadata> {
#        ?g simp:source-relation "IS_ASSOCIATED_WITH" .
#      }
#    }
#  Expected result before this patch: 40864
#
#  VERIFY AFTER: re-run the same SELECT above. Expected result: 0.

PREFIX simp: <urn:simpathic:>

DELETE { GRAPH <urn:simpathic:context:all_metadata> { ?g simp:source-relation "IS_ASSOCIATED_WITH" . } }
INSERT { GRAPH <urn:simpathic:context:all_metadata> { ?g simp:source-relation "ASSOCIATED_WITH" . } }
WHERE {
  GRAPH <urn:simpathic:context:all_metadata> {
    ?g simp:source-relation "IS_ASSOCIATED_WITH" .
  }
}
